## 3. 2026 DESIGN FOUNDATIONS (apply by default, not as options)

- **Liquid Glass / Glassmorphism 2.0:** favor refined, subtle translucent
  layering over the heavy-blur glass of the early 2020s — pair translucency
  with soft noise texture, a gradient border, and layered shadow for a
  dimensional (not flat-frosted) finish. Reserve it for overlays, navbars,
  and cards — never wash an entire page in glass.
- **Motion systems over isolated micro-interactions:** treat transitions,
  loading states, and feedback animations as one connected system so the
  whole journey feels continuous, not like a pile of separate effects.
- **Bento grids:** default layout for feature lists, dashboards, and pricing —
  modular, asymmetric card groups that present dense content without
  overwhelming the eye.
- **Spatial depth on 2D screens:** use elevation, overlap, scale, and distance
  intentionally to signal what's primary vs. secondary — depth as an
  information hierarchy tool, not just visual flair.
- **Dark-mode-first:** design the dark theme first, then derive light mode —
  never bolt dark mode on afterward. Avoid pure `#000`; use near-black
  (`#0A0A0B`–`#121214`) so glass/shadow layers read correctly.
- **Variable & kinetic typography:** load one variable font file per family;
  use fluid weight/optical-size interpolation instead of swapping static
  files; reserve kinetic (animating/morphing) type for hero moments only.

