## 6. LAYOUT & SPACING

- Generous whitespace: section padding `py-20 md:py-32`, container padding
  `px-6 md:px-10 lg:px-20`, gaps `gap-6 md:gap-12`.
- Max content width `max-w-7xl` centered; intentional asymmetry allowed in
  hero and bento sections.
- 8px spacing scale — no arbitrary one-off pixel values.

---

## 7. BACKGROUNDS, DEPTH & GLASSMORPHISM

- No flat, single-color section backgrounds. Default to one of:
  - Animated mesh gradient (slow-drifting radial blobs, `blur-3xl`, low opacity)
  - Floating gradient blobs on a subtle loop (Framer Motion `animate` with
    `repeat: Infinity`, `ease: "easeInOut"`)
  - Fine noise/grid texture overlay at very low opacity for tactile depth
- Standard glass card recipe:
  ```css
  .glass-card {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);
    backdrop-filter: blur(20px);
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(20px);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
    border-radius: 16px;
    box-shadow: 0 20px 40px -12px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.25);
  }
  ```
  In Tailwind: `bg-white/5 backdrop-blur-xl border border-white/10 shadow-2xl shadow-black/20`.
- Subtlety is the rule, not the exception — excessive transparency kills
  readability. Test every glass surface against light AND dark content
  scrolling behind it.
- Provide a `backdrop-filter` fallback (solid `bg-surface/95`) for older
  browsers/low-power devices.

