## 9. COMPONENT-SPECIFIC RULES

- **Hero:** Lottie/3D/animated-SVG centerpiece + animated gradient background +
  staggered headline/subtext/CTA reveal.
- **Skills/Features:** interactive bento grid OR smooth infinite marquee
  (`will-change: transform`, pause-on-hover), each item with icon/Lottie,
  glow-on-hover border, staggered entry.
- **Navbar:** sticky glass, condenses (height/blur) on scroll via a
  scroll-position hook. Mobile: animated slide-in drawer or bottom sheet.
- **Forms:** floating labels, animated focus rings, inline validation with
  motion (shake on error, checkmark morph on success).
- **Footer:** background consistent with hero; newsletter/CTA in a distinct
  glass card.

---

## 10. RESPONSIVE & ACCESSIBILITY

- Mobile-first: build `base`/`sm` layout first, layer `md:`/`lg:`/`xl:` after.
- Complex nav collapses into animated drawers/bottom sheets below `md:`.
- Touch targets ≥ 44px.
- Visible focus states on every interactive element
  (`focus-visible:ring-2 ring-offset-2`) — glass surfaces must not swallow them.
- WCAG 2.1 AA+ checklist to satisfy on every component: sufficient contrast in
  all states, color never the sole indicator of meaning, full keyboard
  navigation, screen-reader labels on icon-only controls, motion can be
  disabled, text resizes to 200% without breaking layout.
- Semantic HTML + ARIA (`role="dialog"` + focus trap for modals,
  `aria-expanded`/`aria-current` for nav).

---

## 11. ASSET SOURCING RULES

- Stock photography: royalty-free only (Unsplash, Pexels) — always
  color-grade/crop to match the palette, never leave a raw stock color cast.
- Icons: `lucide-react` for UI; custom SVG only for brand marks.
- Lottie files: keep under ~150KB, lazy-load with no SSR.
- GIFs: avoid where Lottie/CSS/Framer Motion can replace them (smaller,
  scalable, themeable). Use real video only for recorded footage/demos,
  served as compressed `.webm`/`.mp4` with a `poster` fallback — not GIF.
- 3D assets: prototype in Spline for speed; move to React Three Fiber for
  production control and performance tuning.

---

## 12. PERFORMANCE GUARDRAILS

- Lazy-load below-the-fold sections, Lottie/3D players, and carousels
  (`dynamic(() => import(...), { ssr: false })`).
- Animate `transform`/`opacity` only.
- Responsive-serve all images with correct `sizes`.
- Keep the hero-path JS bundle lean — defer non-critical animation/3D libs.

